00:25:13.130 --> 00:25:15.210
to your point, Shelley it
took me time to realize

00:25:15.210 --> 00:25:17.590
Oh, this is what I'm attracted to.

00:25:17.590 --> 00:25:19.877
You know, the internet kids
that I was investing in 2005

00:25:19.877 --> 00:25:22.070
and 2006, they were the underdogs.

00:25:22.070 --> 00:25:23.920
- Right.
- A hundred percent

00:25:23.920 --> 00:25:27.320
- They were nerds, wasn't
cool, nobody believed.

00:25:27.320 --> 00:25:30.270
Now it's completely in the other chasm

00:25:30.270 --> 00:25:32.250
which is why I've lost my spirit for it.

00:25:32.250 --> 00:25:33.390
So for everybody's listening,

00:25:33.390 --> 00:25:35.170
find where your spirit is,

00:25:35.170 --> 00:25:37.640
because that's going to
allow you to go deeper.

00:25:37.640 --> 00:25:40.260
- Hundred percent (indistinct)

00:25:40.260 --> 00:25:42.320
hope that we're going
to bring him right now.

00:25:42.320 --> 00:25:45.520
I would love to welcome Mindy Grossman,

00:25:45.520 --> 00:25:47.763
who is the CEO of WW.

00:25:48.740 --> 00:25:50.300
- Hi guys.
- Hey

00:25:50.300 --> 00:25:51.890
It was like the perfect clue

00:25:51.890 --> 00:25:54.380
when Gary was going on, Gary V,

00:25:54.380 --> 00:25:56.420
about the people we believe in

00:25:56.420 --> 00:25:59.680
and the people that can build
a business, drive a business

00:25:59.680 --> 00:26:00.780
not just inherit one,

00:26:00.780 --> 00:26:05.700
but create one based on
passion and power and money

00:26:05.700 --> 00:26:06.800
and all of those things.

00:26:06.800 --> 00:26:09.310
There is no one better
to reflect those values

00:26:09.310 --> 00:26:10.143
than you Mindy.

00:26:10.143 --> 00:26:11.960
We are so excited to have you here.

00:26:11.960 --> 00:26:12.793
- Thank you.

00:26:12.793 --> 00:26:15.280
And Gary, I love what you
just said about self esteem

00:26:15.280 --> 00:26:16.270
and self awareness.

00:26:16.270 --> 00:26:18.840
I always say, particularly to women,

00:26:18.840 --> 00:26:21.642
self-awareness is your
greatest super power.

00:26:21.642 --> 00:26:24.530
And it's just so important.

00:26:24.530 --> 00:26:26.810
And that belief in yourself,

00:26:26.810 --> 00:26:30.590
comes from extreme awareness.

00:26:30.590 --> 00:26:33.720
- But Mindy, where did that
extreme awareness for you?

00:26:33.720 --> 00:26:35.420
Was there a pivot moment?

00:26:35.420 --> 00:26:38.630
Was there one of those
heartbeat moments that you had,

00:26:38.630 --> 00:26:41.070
that said, you know, cause
you've risen the ranks,

00:26:41.070 --> 00:26:43.720
you've won every accolade
of most powerful women

00:26:43.720 --> 00:26:46.800
on fortune Forbes on,
you know, and everything.

00:26:46.800 --> 00:26:51.290
Was there a moment in
your career that you found

00:26:51.290 --> 00:26:54.280
that confidence kind of emanated from you?

00:26:54.280 --> 00:26:56.750
You said I got this and I can do anything-

00:26:56.750 --> 00:26:58.470
- You know I thinks it's been a journey.

00:26:58.470 --> 00:27:00.993
I think it's been a journey
that's really built.

00:27:01.830 --> 00:27:04.657
You know, I took a risk
very early in my career.

00:27:04.657 --> 00:27:06.640
You know, I was supposed to be a lawyer.

00:27:06.640 --> 00:27:08.000
I was supposed to get married.

00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:10.470
And at the last minute

00:27:10.470 --> 00:27:12.037
in my last semester of college

00:27:12.037 --> 00:27:14.380
and I started college at 16.

00:27:14.380 --> 00:27:16.370
I just decided to change my life.

00:27:16.370 --> 00:27:19.890
And I moved to New York at 20, in 1977.

00:27:19.890 --> 00:27:22.520
Broke my engagement, decided
not to go to law school

00:27:22.520 --> 00:27:24.620
instead, I'm going to figure it out.

00:27:24.620 --> 00:27:28.720
So I always say not taking the
risk would have been riskier.

00:27:28.720 --> 00:27:32.330
So it definitely gave me the confidence

00:27:32.330 --> 00:27:33.540
and a lot of what I did.

00:27:33.540 --> 00:27:35.200
But when I moved to New York,

00:27:35.200 --> 00:27:36.980
I had no finances.

00:27:36.980 --> 00:27:40.282
I didn't have no parental support.

00:27:40.282 --> 00:27:43.350
You know, they didn't
have the wherewithal.

00:27:43.350 --> 00:27:46.780
And so it was really about
my taking care of myself.

00:27:46.780 --> 00:27:48.050
And I would say,

00:27:48.050 --> 00:27:50.550
that the one thing in the first few years,

00:27:50.550 --> 00:27:54.930
that I didn't do enough of
was think about security.

00:27:54.930 --> 00:27:58.180
It was you know, spend what you have.

00:27:58.180 --> 00:28:00.140
And then as I got older

00:28:00.140 --> 00:28:02.790
and I understood the business skills,

00:28:02.790 --> 00:28:05.410
I said I'm not applying
my business skills,

00:28:05.410 --> 00:28:07.220
to my personal life.

00:28:07.220 --> 00:28:09.480
And I need to be as focused,

00:28:09.480 --> 00:28:11.880
as educated and aware

00:28:11.880 --> 00:28:15.560
as I am in business in
my personal finances.

00:28:15.560 --> 00:28:18.389
And that was a big moment for me.

00:28:18.389 --> 00:28:21.010
And then when I got married,

00:28:21.010 --> 00:28:24.080
I'm married to a mathematical physicist

00:28:24.080 --> 00:28:26.890
who is a financial expert. Right.

00:28:26.890 --> 00:28:31.290
But I wasn't going to
abdicate my intentions,

00:28:31.290 --> 00:28:32.960
my right and my understanding

00:28:32.960 --> 00:28:35.560
of where I wanted to go with finances.

00:28:35.560 --> 00:28:40.250
So we've been partners in
this journey the whole time.

00:28:40.250 --> 00:28:42.060
And I think one of the
wake up calls for me

00:28:42.060 --> 00:28:43.940
is I had a girlfriend,

00:28:43.940 --> 00:28:47.140
who's very sadly her
husband all of a sudden

00:28:47.140 --> 00:28:48.880
died on the racquetball court.

00:28:48.880 --> 00:28:51.870
And she had no idea where anything was,

00:28:51.870 --> 00:28:55.440
their finances, what their status was.

00:28:55.440 --> 00:28:58.880
And I remember saying that
should happen to no one,

00:28:58.880 --> 00:29:02.620
you know, you should be
the owner of what it is

00:29:02.620 --> 00:29:05.500
your goals are and everything else.

00:29:05.500 --> 00:29:08.223
Now that doesn't mean
you can't have a partner,

00:29:08.223 --> 00:29:13.223
but you need to be as educated, informed,

00:29:13.940 --> 00:29:15.440
you need to make the right decisions

00:29:15.440 --> 00:29:17.513
whether they be about an investment,

00:29:18.400 --> 00:29:21.570
or whether they be about
what you want to save

00:29:21.570 --> 00:29:22.840
versus what you want to make

00:29:22.840 --> 00:29:25.590
and Hope I was listening
to you as well earlier,

00:29:25.590 --> 00:29:27.240
everything is individual.

00:29:27.240 --> 00:29:29.080
Whether it's a level of risk,

00:29:29.080 --> 00:29:31.590
or you know what you are comfortable with

00:29:31.590 --> 00:29:34.700
and what your joint plans are.

00:29:34.700 --> 00:29:37.250
And so throughout, you
know, our relationship,

00:29:37.250 --> 00:29:38.860
even to this day,

00:29:38.860 --> 00:29:43.800
we are both very involved
in whatever decisions

00:29:43.800 --> 00:29:46.580
that we're making together.

00:29:46.580 --> 00:29:49.020
And we certainly have our own individual

00:29:49.020 --> 00:29:50.320
investment decisions.

00:29:50.320 --> 00:29:54.700
And the other point you made
that I thought was really smart

00:29:54.700 --> 00:29:58.890
is any startup investment I make,

00:29:58.890 --> 00:30:01.870
I assume I'm going to get nothing back.

00:30:01.870 --> 00:30:05.058
Now, I do it because I
believe in the people-

00:30:05.058 --> 00:30:05.891
- And you might win

00:30:05.891 --> 00:30:08.000
- Just like Gary believed in Rachel

00:30:09.230 --> 00:30:13.380
You believe in the person and
you will lend your support.

00:30:13.380 --> 00:30:15.690
So, you know, I made the decision

00:30:15.690 --> 00:30:18.800
to start investing in some early stage

00:30:18.800 --> 00:30:20.880
women founded businesses

00:30:20.880 --> 00:30:24.270
and said I can give
them, you know, capital

00:30:24.270 --> 00:30:26.713
but I can also give them support.

00:30:27.710 --> 00:30:31.490
And so if it works great, and if not

00:30:31.490 --> 00:30:35.750
I did my best to help
support the investment

00:30:35.750 --> 00:30:36.583
- Mindy, real quick.

00:30:36.583 --> 00:30:38.240
You played at the highest levels

00:30:38.240 --> 00:30:42.590
of business in this world.

00:30:42.590 --> 00:30:44.300
Do you think that financial literacy,

00:30:44.300 --> 00:30:47.070
because the story you told
about the racquet ball

00:30:47.070 --> 00:30:48.900
a gentlemen, which is devastating,

00:30:48.900 --> 00:30:51.690
is such a common story.

00:30:51.690 --> 00:30:56.360
For the women of the
50s, 60s, 70s, 80s, 90s.

00:30:56.360 --> 00:31:00.340
You know, and I think there
has been a turn thank God.

00:31:00.340 --> 00:31:02.790
But as you were talking, literally,

00:31:02.790 --> 00:31:04.800
I was like how many of the guys,

00:31:04.800 --> 00:31:07.600
that were at the racquetball
guys that died also,

00:31:07.600 --> 00:31:10.030
had no like physical literacy.

00:31:10.030 --> 00:31:11.450
Like when you think about physical,

00:31:11.450 --> 00:31:14.280
like financial money
literacy across the board,

00:31:14.280 --> 00:31:16.860
because you interact so
heavily across the board,

00:31:16.860 --> 00:31:19.720
do you agree with my assumptions that like

00:31:19.720 --> 00:31:21.920
in general people's
relationship with money

00:31:21.920 --> 00:31:25.820
and even more so women
is just stunningly low.

00:31:25.820 --> 00:31:28.920
- Absolutely. I think financial literacy

00:31:28.920 --> 00:31:32.411
could be a prerequisite,
as much as you need ABCs.

00:31:32.411 --> 00:31:33.410
- I agree.
- Right?

00:31:33.410 --> 00:31:36.430
- So Mindy, shouldn't it be taught?

00:31:36.430 --> 00:31:37.380
Shouldn't it be taught?

00:31:37.380 --> 00:31:41.050
Like they used to teach,
they don't teach...

00:31:41.050 --> 00:31:42.160
They basic...

00:31:42.160 --> 00:31:42.993
And I don't even want to-

00:31:42.993 --> 00:31:44.533
I don't like calling a financial literacy.

00:31:44.533 --> 00:31:47.210
Because I think that scares people, right?

00:31:47.210 --> 00:31:49.476
- It's a scary word.

00:31:49.476 --> 00:31:52.160
- It's a scary word.

00:31:52.160 --> 00:31:53.190
- Can we call it,

00:31:53.190 --> 00:31:55.283
know what to do with your fucking money?

00:31:55.283 --> 00:31:58.009
(laughs)

00:31:58.009 --> 00:32:01.130
(indistinct)

00:32:01.130 --> 00:32:02.860
- You know, I didn't even have,

00:32:02.860 --> 00:32:05.780
the certain other classes I need to take.

00:32:05.780 --> 00:32:08.000
And I, you know, for example,

00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:10.730
you know, when I really went into business

00:32:10.730 --> 00:32:14.590
and started up the ranks
and really owning P &amp; Ls,

00:32:14.590 --> 00:32:17.030
I said, I really need
to be further educated.

00:32:17.030 --> 00:32:20.910
And I went to take the executive
program at Harvard, right?

00:32:20.910 --> 00:32:24.210
So why aren't we educating
ourselves about the business?

00:32:24.210 --> 00:32:27.040
And we're not spending as
much time educating ourselves

00:32:27.040 --> 00:32:29.570
about our financial future.

00:32:29.570 --> 00:32:31.150
And you need to do both.

00:32:31.150 --> 00:32:33.580
And I so agree it needs to be,

00:32:33.580 --> 00:32:37.070
whatever you want to call the curricula.

00:32:37.070 --> 00:32:39.313
It needs to be a prerequisite.

00:32:40.150 --> 00:32:41.070
- And that's a whole thing.

00:32:41.070 --> 00:32:44.550
So you went, you actually
took the initiative to go,

00:32:44.550 --> 00:32:48.920
and lifelong learner go and
understand it better. Right?

00:32:48.920 --> 00:32:51.970
You took that, but
we've got to help people

00:32:51.970 --> 00:32:54.580
understand that they got to do it earlier.

00:32:54.580 --> 00:32:56.820
If this is not calculus, right?

00:32:56.820 --> 00:32:59.220
This is not complicated math, right?

00:32:59.220 --> 00:33:02.490
You don't have to move from a
balance sheet to a cash flow,

00:33:02.490 --> 00:33:04.000
- I always look around,

00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:06.770
having that class would have done more

00:33:06.770 --> 00:33:08.860
for most people than calculus.

00:33:08.860 --> 00:33:09.693
- But I also-

00:33:09.693 --> 00:33:10.990
- I got married to a mathematician.

00:33:10.990 --> 00:33:12.740
So he gets a little upset when I say that.

00:33:12.740 --> 00:33:16.070
- But I also think having
that class with contextual

00:33:16.070 --> 00:33:19.790
real life experiences also helps a lot.

00:33:19.790 --> 00:33:23.070
If you just read it in
isolation in a book,

00:33:23.070 --> 00:33:26.400
would you really have
gained the same value

00:33:26.400 --> 00:33:29.620
as having to live in
breathe managing cashflow

00:33:29.620 --> 00:33:32.947
and liquidity and investment in that.

00:33:32.947 --> 00:33:36.689
- And I do think that
particularly for women,

00:33:36.689 --> 00:33:40.780
we need to educate ourselves
to have the confidence

00:33:40.780 --> 00:33:43.770
to make the investment decisions.

00:33:43.770 --> 00:33:47.030
And, you know, I'm sure you've
brought it up all the time.

00:33:47.030 --> 00:33:49.290
We make 90% of the purchase decisions

00:33:49.290 --> 00:33:52.480
and just a small percentage
of the investment decisions.

00:33:52.480 --> 00:33:56.470
And women need to be better
advocates for themselves

00:33:56.470 --> 00:33:59.130
and not abdicate their responsibility.

00:33:59.130 --> 00:34:01.923
Because it's so critical.

00:34:01.923 --> 00:34:05.190
You know, even if you're you're partnering

00:34:05.190 --> 00:34:09.250
but let's say you're just building your...

00:34:09.250 --> 00:34:11.380
What you need in your career

00:34:11.380 --> 00:34:13.440
and what you want in your life,

00:34:13.440 --> 00:34:15.670
setting those goals and having those plans

00:34:15.670 --> 00:34:20.670
and understanding the risks
that you're open to taking

00:34:21.350 --> 00:34:23.820
and what investment decisions

00:34:23.820 --> 00:34:27.480
at some point do you need
to start thinking about,

00:34:27.480 --> 00:34:28.853
that's education.

00:34:30.170 --> 00:34:33.050
- So Mindy, I couldn't agree.

00:34:33.050 --> 00:34:37.980
You also talked about coming
out and in from college.

00:34:37.980 --> 00:34:42.880
Nope. I too, didn't get married
the first time so to speak,

00:34:42.880 --> 00:34:46.440
I walked away and you have
to own it yourself. Right?

00:34:46.440 --> 00:34:49.750
And that sends you and
Gary you talk often about-

00:34:49.750 --> 00:34:51.920
- Can I ask Hope, I'm
sorry to interrupt you.

00:34:51.920 --> 00:34:54.200
The fact that you and Mindy
have this shared experience,

00:34:54.200 --> 00:34:55.730
is, you know really-

00:34:55.730 --> 00:34:57.610
- Even I do by the way.

00:34:57.610 --> 00:34:59.013
- You too Shell?
- Yeah.

00:35:00.210 --> 00:35:01.043
- This is just really interesting to me,

00:35:01.043 --> 00:35:03.010
because I think all the good for me

00:35:03.010 --> 00:35:05.763
has been under social studies and history.

00:35:07.490 --> 00:35:08.810
Very simple question.

00:35:08.810 --> 00:35:10.680
Was that commonly happening

00:35:10.680 --> 00:35:13.070
for strong women in your generation?

